  - title: LEVEL 22 | Forward vs Reverse Bias
    explanation: 'FORWARD TEST: D1 anode toward the 330 Ohm resistor and banded cathode
      toward LED anode. With switch closed, conventional current flows and green
      LED illuminates. REVERSE TEST: Power off before swapping D1 wires. Connect
      resistor to D1 cathode and D1 anode to LED anode; current should be blocked
      and LED should stay off. The schematic depicts the forward-bias SOLUTION; reverse
      bias is an experiment, not an additional simultaneous electrical branch.'
    caption: PAGE 3/4 | FORWARD = GREEN LED ON | REVERSE = OFF
    parts:
    - id: battery
      kind: 0
      position: {x: 0.1, y: 0.52}
      label: 5 V
      color: {r: 0.98, g: 0.29, b: 0.35, a: 1}
